        <div class="fji-answer-block"><h3>Fujiiryoki vs. Osaki</h3><p>Osaki delivers more features per dollar and stronger intensity &mdash; particularly through their Duo dual-engine lineup. Fujiiryoki delivers more precision, refined Japanese craftsmanship, and a quieter premium identity. Choose Fujiiryoki for quality of feel; Osaki for feature breadth and assertive power.</p></div>
        <div class="fji-answer-block"><h3>Fujiiryoki vs. Infinity</h3><p>Infinity offers their proprietary Syner-D tandem-roller technology and stretch-dominant profiles. Fujiiryoki offers Japanese precision engineering and a more controlled, human-feeling massage. Both serve daily users well; the feel is distinctly different. Try both at our showroom.</p></div>
        <div class="fji-answer-block"><h3>Fujiiryoki vs. Ogawa</h3><p>Both position as premium, quality-conscious brands. Ogawa leans more toward luxury aesthetics and design integration; Fujiiryoki leans more toward Japanese engineering precision. Buyers who value form often lean Ogawa; buyers who value function-first legacy lean Fujiiryoki.</p></div>
        <div class="fji-answer-block"><h3>Fujiiryoki vs. Cozzia</h3><p>Cozzia offers VarioMotion technology and a broader five-model tier ladder. Fujiiryoki offers more focused Japanese craftsmanship positioning. Both appeal to quality-feel buyers; the distinction lies in brand philosophy &mdash; American-market engineering vs. Japanese heritage precision.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

